        <mxCell id="guard" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;Account guard: none in code.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; tfctl.sh, init.sh and the provider never compare the caller's account; the state bucket in the env file decides it in practice. Cluster admin follows whoever runs Terraform: an apply of cluster/eks through terraform.yml (lane 3) would move the admin entry to opsfleet-terraform-apply-role." style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#232F3E;verticalAlign=top;spacingRight=6;container=1;collapsible=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#879196;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=3;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="acct">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="766" width="2576" height="44" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oidc" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;Every row&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: the job asks GitHub for an OIDC token with audience sts.amazonaws.com and calls sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity. STS checks the token against the account's IAM OIDC provider token.actions.githubusercontent.com (system/iam/github-oidc: created when create_provider is on, otherwise read) and against the role's trust condition on the token's sub claim." style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#232F3E;verticalAlign=top;spacingRight=6;container=1;collapsible=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#879196;align=left;spacingLeft=50;spacingTop=3;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="acct">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="876" width="2880" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
