        <mxCell id="role_a_i" value="" style="sketch=0;outlineConnect=0;fontColor=#232F3E;gradientColor=none;fillColor=#DD344C;strokeColor=none;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=10;aspect=fixed;pointerEvents=1;shape=mxgraph.aws4.role;dashed=0;" vertex="1" parent="role_a">
          <mxGeometry x="8" y="8" width="30" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="act_a" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;plan job&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: Vault JWT login (Vault role opsfleet-plan) exports the common values, the account id among them, and the stack's own values; assume the plan role; ./tfctl.sh &amp;lt;tier&amp;gt; plan &amp;lt;stack&amp;gt;; the run summary keeps resource addresses and totals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;apply job&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: needs plan; Vault role opsfleet-apply; assume the apply role; ./tfctl.sh &amp;lt;tier&amp;gt; apply &amp;lt;stack&amp;gt; --auto-approve." style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#232F3E;verticalAlign=top;spacingRight=6;container=1;collapsible=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#879196;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=3;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="acct">
          <mxGeometry x="920" y="962" width="1060" height="112" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
